ded during the run.\n\nEnd-state, measured with query_snapshot after the last place step (placement frames are re-read because they ride on base1):\n- u_brown: 0.0022 m from u_brown_placement (tolerance 0.01).\n- u_orange: 0.0021 m (tolerance 0.02).\n- line_green: 0.0066 m (tolerance 0.015).\n- inverted_u_yellow: 0.0013 m (tolerance 0.012).\n- Orientations match within about 0.5°.\n\nProcess evidence:\n- Each pick lifted its part 0.20–0.30 m (requirement ≥0.05).\n- Grasp widths were within 0.0042 m of each step's declared width, and plateau efforts were 11–32, well above the 0.05 air-close floor.\n- Per-part clamp-effort monitors were armed at each part's own max_clamp_effort (100/200/170/250) and never fired; sampled peaks were about 55–64.\n- The in-hand slip monitor (grasp_slip_tolerance 0.02) never fired.\n- Five bystanders and base1 were monitored for the whole run against disturbance_tolerance 0.02. The inactive-parts monitor re-baselined each part after release. Neither fired.\n- At run end the bystanders are within 0.00002 m of their run-start poses. base1 sits 0.0079 m from its run-start pose, almost entirely in y, and was already 0.0089 m off by the end of place_u_brown. I judge this to be seating contact nudging the fixture. It is within tolerance and the placement frames moved with it, so it is not a finding.\n- Executor end_step reports were never used as evidence; every figure above is my own measurement.\n\nNotes:\n- line_green sits about 6.5 mm below its frame, presumably deeper in its slot. That is within tolerance.\n- For effects.object_tcp_offset_m I treated the clause as tracking stability (offset change while held), because the absolute part-origin-to-TCP distance (~0.09 m) is fixed geometry. That interpretation is mine, and the slip monitor is what evidences it.\n- All 12 step_ids matched the expected process; there were no unplanned steps.\n\nWorkspace: observation obs-001 records an unlisted small red/orange cube at roughly world (0.08, -0.39